      "round_summary": "Round 1 (v2): Fixed assertion `req_ack_not_concurrent` (assertion_error). Root cause: `!(req && io.ack)` is too strict — LFSR drives req independently, can be high when FSM asserts ack. Fix: use `ra.io.start` (exposed IO from ReqAck, asserted when state=starting) to capture the triggering req via `RegNext(req)`, tracking only the req that started the current transaction. Avoids accessing internal `ra.state` which is not cross-module visible in Chisel. Assertion label preserved. No homologous assertions found.",
