      "round": 2,
      "round_summary": "Round 2: Fixed DUT race condition for assertion `req_ack_not_concurrent` (dut_bug). Root cause: `when(io.ack) { reqTriggered := false.B }` uses non-blocking assignment, so at the cycle `io.ack` fires, `reqTriggered` is still 1 when the combinational assertion evaluates — creating a Verilog race condition. Fix: changed clear from `io.ack` to `ra.io.ready` (which goes high one cycle before `io.ack`, when the slave count reaches 3). This ensures `reqTriggered` is stably 0 by the time `io.ack` evaluates. Assertion label `req_ack_not_concurrent` preserved. No homologous assertions found (the structurally similar `pendingReq` pattern uses a different assertion semantics — `assertImplies` reads `pendingReq` before its non-blocking clear, which is correct for that property).",
